# Line endings are LF in the repository, always.
#
# Without this, every `git add` on Windows warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF",
# and the Windows + Linux CI matrix starts comparing files that differ only in
# line endings. The matrix exists to catch real portability defects; CRLF noise
# inside it teaches people to ignore the matrix.
*         text=auto eol=lf

# Git runs these two through /bin/sh. A CRLF after the shebang makes the
# interpreter unfindable — on Git for Windows the hook dies with a message that
# does not say why.
.githooks/pre-commit  text eol=lf
.githooks/commit-msg  text eol=lf

*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.ico     binary
*.webp    binary
*.avif    binary
*.woff2   binary

# The database is a build product, never a source file. Marked binary so a
# stray commit of one cannot be "merged".
*.db      binary
